    {
      "id": "bridge-editor-instructions",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Bridge Editor Sketch",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -2060,
        "y": 260
      },
      "width": 760,
      "height": 300,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "guided-by",
          "key": "guided-by",
          "label": "guided by",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 180,
          "role": "relationship",
          "allowedEdgeTypes": [
            "reference"
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "relationship": true,
            "role": "relationship"
          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "bridge-editor"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Bridge Editor (sketch)\n\nThe editor a Bridge node opens with its pencil. Sections are illustrative.\n\n## Export Bridge\n\n- **Target:** the graph this Bridge exports to, and its role.\n- **What it exposes:** views, resources and declarations, as today.\n- **Events:** a checkbox for each event this graph declares, and one row per class with its members underneath. Exposure keys for events that no longer exist are kept, with a Forget action.\n- **Effective exposure:** what a neighbor can actually see.\n- **Status:** what is missing and why.\n\n## Import Bridge\n\n- **Target:** the neighbor this Bridge consumes.\n- **What the neighbor exposes:** read live from the neighbor.\n- **Events:** for each exposed event (or class), the Handler that answers it, chosen from Handlers in this graph, with the subscription stored on this Bridge.\n- **Unresolved subscriptions:** kept as authored, with the reason and an explicit Remove.\n- **Status:** what is missing and why.\n\n## The Properties panel\n\nGeneric node concerns only, plus a link that opens the Bridge Editor.\n\n## One data path\n\nExposure and subscriptions are written only through the existing planners, so the Bridge Editor and the Handler editor cannot disagree."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        }
      },
      "handles": [
