      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "A Bridge Is Edited on the Bridge",
        "statement": "Everything a Bridge does should be editable from the Bridge's own editor, the one its pencil opens: its target and role, what it exposes, what it consumes, and how the graph reacts to the Events that cross it. The Properties panel goes back to generic node concerns. Export and import Bridges get sections shaped to their role, with diagnostics that say what is missing and why.",
        "status": "framed",
        "confidence": "unproven",
        "notes": "Events and their reactions are the newest thing a Bridge does. They follow github://mikemartinez1974/public/tasks/bridge-owned-event-subscriptions/root.node, where Import Bridges own subscriptions and Export Bridges own exposure. The editor is shown on the Bridge's card, as an Event Handler's is, and not in a side panel.",
        "definitionKey": "idea",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "idea",
          "sourceRef": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/idea-template/classes/nodes/idea.node-class.node",
