          "portId": "affects"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Bridge behavior is scattered",
        "statement": "The Bridge's own editor (a hosted Bridge Editor) already carries a label, a note, Target Ref for an import Bridge, and the export policy fields and Export Surface for an export Bridge, plus a Bridge Status block. Role, Kind, Grants, the exposure candidate pickers and the Events UI lived in the Properties panel instead, and the Properties panel also repeated the export policy, so some settings could be edited in two places. A user editing a Bridge had to know to leave its editor, right-click for Properties, and find them. The Events section was nested under Behavior, after a long Setup block, until it was given its own section.",
        "impact": "The part of a Bridge that matters most, what crosses it and who answers, is the hardest to find. New event behavior would keep landing in whichever panel is nearest, adding a third home.",
        "urgency": "high",
        "definitionKey": "idea-problem",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "idea-problem",
          "sourceRef": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/idea-template/classes/nodes/idea-problem.node-class.node",
