          "metadata": {
            "relationship": true,
            "role": "relationship"
          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Where Bridge UI lives today",
        "findings": "The Bridge node's editor is a hosted \"bridge-editor\": a structured form with role-specific fields (shown or hidden by the Bridge's role) and a Bridge Status block. The Properties panel held Setup (role, kind), Grants, the exposure candidate pickers, and Events. A Bridge records its role, kind, target and grants in three places (on the node, under bridge and under target), so every write must update all of them. Events are one component that reads a Bridge node plus the graph and writes through planners for exposure and subscriptions, so it does not depend on where it is shown. Bridges expose and consume events one node at a time; class scopes do not cross them yet.",
        "sourceUrl": "github://TwiliteLLC/twilite/components/GraphEditor/components/BridgeEventsPanel.js",
        "sourceType": "prototype",
        "definitionKey": "idea-research",
        "_classBinding": {
